Before the data ever reaches Power BI, the Excel workbook performs a full scoring pipeline using formulas and a custom macro. This ensures that every audit is standardized, validated, and enriched with calculated fields.

1. Accuracy Result Logic
Determines whether the audit passed or failed based on critical misses:

Code
=IF(L2="","",IF(L2>0,"Fail","Pass"))
Interpretation:

If no critical misses → Pass

If one or more critical misses → Fail

This creates the foundational binary outcome used across QC and WFM dashboards.

2. Critical & Important Miss Counters
Counts how many critical or important items were missed:

Code
critical_misses_count: =COUNTA(N2,P2,R2)
important_misses_count: =COUNTA(T2,V2,X2)
Interpretation:

Critical misses live in N, P, R

Important misses live in T, V, X

This feeds directly into error classification and accuracy scoring.

3. Item‑Level Binary Scoring (DV/AL Logic)
You built a dynamic scoring system that assigns 1 = pass and 0 = fail for each item based on call type.

Example:

Code
dv_c1_idv_reviewed:
=IF(AND(G2="DV",ISNUMBER(SEARCH("C1",N2&P2&R2&T2&V2&X2))),0,1)
Interpretation:

If the call type is DV

AND the missed items contain “C1”

→ Score = 0 (failed)

Otherwise → Score = 1 (passed)

You have this logic replicated for:

DV Critical (dv_c1, dv_c2, dv_c3…)

DV Important (dv_i1, dv_i2…)

AL Critical (al_c1, al_c2…)

AL Important (al_i1, al_i2…)

This is exactly how professional QA scoring engines work.

4. Total Possible Items (DV vs AL)
You dynamically calculate how many items could have been scored:

Code
total_critical_possible: =IF(G2="DV",9,IF(G2="AL",13,""))
total_important_possible: =IF(G2="DV",3,IF(G2="AL",3,""))
This allows you to compute accuracy percentages correctly.

5. Accuracy Calculations (Critical, Important, Weighted)
You built a full accuracy scoring model:

Code
critical_accuracy_rate: =IF(BC2=0,1,(BC2-L2)/BC2)
important_accuracy_rate: =IF(BD2=0,1,(BD2-M2)/BD2)
weighted_accuracy_weight_70_30: =(BE2*0.7)+(BF2*0.3)
Interpretation:

Critical accuracy = (critical possible – critical missed) / critical possible

Important accuracy = same logic

Weighted accuracy = 70% critical + 30% important

This is a professional‑grade scoring model.

6. Error Classification & Summaries
You classify the error type:

Code
error_type: =IFS(L2>0,"Critical",M2>0,"Important",TRUE,"NA")
And generate a full missed‑item summary:

Code
missed_items_summary: =IF(COUNTA(N2:Y2)=0,"NA",TEXTJOIN(",",TRUE,N2:Y2))
This powers your Supervisor dashboard’s “First Missed Item” and “Missed Item Summary” tables.

